      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000",
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Hilbert Index → Tile X/Y\n\nTurns a single integer into `x`/`y` along a Hilbert curve, wired into the saver's\n`x`/`y` with **coords_mode = manual**.\n\n`PrimitiveInt` above holds the index with its control set to **increment**, so\nevery queue advances one step along the curve: consecutive renders land next to\neach other on the map *and* contiguously inside the archive, because PMTiles\norders its tiles by the same curve.\n\n### Inputs\n\n- **index** — position along the curve. Wraps at `4^order`.\n- **order** — the grid is `2^order` tiles a side; use the same value as the\n  saver's `z`.\n- **block_size** — tiles per render (a 1024 px render at 256 px tiles is 4). The\n  curve then walks *blocks* instead of tiles, so multi-tile renders cannot\n  overlap.\n\n### Outputs\n\n- **x**, **y** — top-left tile of the block.\n- **info** — the mapping, as text.\n\nAt `z=5` with 4×4-tile renders the curve is order 3, and indices 0–3 give\n(0,0) (0,4) (4,4) (4,0) — the curve's first \"U\".\n"
      ]
    }
